or the I.CO.N.A. Study Group</collab></person-group><article-title>Economic evaluation of HIV treatments: the I.CO.N.A. Cohort study</article-title><source>Health Policy</source><year>2005</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>304</fpage><lpage>313</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16226140</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.healthpol.2005.01.016</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sendi</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Schellenberg</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Ungsedhapand</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaufmann</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bucher</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Weber</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Battegay</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><collab>Swiss HIV Cohort Study</collab></person-group><article-title>Productivity costs and determinants of productivity in HIV-infected patients</article-title><source>Clin Ther</source><year>2004</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>791</fpage><lpage>800</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15220024</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0149-2918(04)90080-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oliva</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Roa</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>del Llano</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Indirect costs in ambulatory patients with HIV/AIDS in Spain: a pilot study</article-title><source>Pharmacoeconomics</source><year>2003</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>1113</fpage><lpage>1121</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14596630</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2165/00019053-200321150-00005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citati